/-!
# The comparison of Stacks 08JP at the standard model, with its natural transformation built

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/EtaleCohomology/SmallEtaleDerivedSheafHomComparisonIso.lean`
proves that the comparison `ε^* R𝓗om_{𝒪_S}(E, F) ⟶ R𝓗om_𝒪(ε^* E, ε^* F)` of Stacks 08JP is an
isomorphism for `E` in the thick triangulated closure of the structure sheaf, over an *assumed*
natural transformation `η` and with the source right unitor and the naturality of the source
bijection carried as hypotheses. This file proves the same two conclusions with all of the
source side discharged:

* the comparison, as a function of `E`, *is* a natural transformation,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonNatTrans`, namely
  `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.MixedTranspose.homComparisonNatTrans`, built from
  the two clauses of Stacks 08J8 for each of the two tensor–internal-Hom bijections; on the source
  side both clauses are proved (`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_zariski`,
  `tensorHomEquivDinatural_zariski`);
* the source right unitor `K ⊗^L_{𝒪_S} 𝒪_S ≅ K` and its naturality are
  `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.rightUnitorAtUnit` and
  `rightUnitorAtUnit_naturality` at the ringed space underlying `S`;
* the shift data of the two factors `ε^*` and `Λ` of the two sides are proved
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.commShift_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel` and its
  three companions).

What remains hypothetical is the target side: the right unitor `r₂` of the target derived tensor
product with its naturality, the two clauses of Stacks 08J8 for the mixed bijection `e₂`, the
unitality of `m`, the shift and triangulated structure of the contravariant derived internal Hom
of each of the two sites, and the shift compatibility of the natural transformation. None of
these asserts that any instance of the comparison is invertible; the only invertibility used is
at `E = 𝒪_S`, and that is proved.

The hypothesis on `E` — generation by `𝒪_S` — is *stronger* than perfection, the hypothesis of
case (2) of Stacks 08JP, and strictly so on a general scheme (on `𝐏¹`, `𝒪(-1)` is perfect and not
in the thick closure of `𝒪`); what is available in the usable direction is the global strictly
perfect case, `isIso_derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison_isStrictlyPerfect`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.zariskiSingleUnit`: the structure sheaf `𝒪_S` as an object of
  `D(𝒪_S)` at the `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedProjectionFormula.singleUnit` spelling.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonNatTrans`: the comparison at the
  standard model as a natural transformation of its first argument.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_zariski` and
  `tensorHomEquivDinatural_zariski`: the two clauses of Stacks 08J8 for the bijection of
  Stacks 08DI on the Zariski site of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel_natTrans`:
  the comparison at the standard model is an isomorphism at every `E` generated by `𝒪_S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison_natTrans`:
  the canonical map between the two sides is an isomorphism there.
* `isIso_derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison_isStrictlyPerfect`:
  the same for `E` isomorphic to a strictly perfect complex (Stacks 08C4).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08J8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08J8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08C4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08C4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08CM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08CM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ATI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ATI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPT)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
  Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback
open scoped CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

attribute [local instance 2000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

-- The source-side derived tensor product `internalHomTensorUncurried` is stated on
-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.KFlatDerivedPullback.Modules S.toRingedSpace`, i.e. at the
-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S.toRingedSpace.sheaf` spelling of the structure sheaf,
-- while the instances carrying `Category (DerivedCategory _)` on it are keyed at the
-- `structureSheafRing` spelling. The two are the same sheaf of rings by `rfl`, but
-- `structureSheafRing` is semireducible and so is not unfolded when the goal is keyed into the
-- instance discrimination tree; reaching the common normal form from the `Tensor.ringSheaf`
-- side instead needs these two Mathlib defs unfolded, which is what this does. This is the
-- same opt-in that
-- `StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.DerivedPushforward.InternalHomPullbackMap`, where
-- these functors are built, carries for the same reason.
attribute [local instance_reducible] CategoryTheory.sheafCompose
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafedSpace.sheaf

/-! ### Stacks 08J8 for the derived internal Hom of the Zariski site of `S` -/

section Zariski

variable (S : Scheme.{u})

/-- **The bijection of Stacks 08DI on the Zariski site of `S` is natural in its source
variable.** This is `tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_ringedSpace` at the ringed space underlying `S`,
read at the `tensorHomEquiv` spelling of the bijection: the two spellings are the same family of
additive equivalences, since `Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHomTensorEquiv` *is*
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCurryHomEquiv` at the site of opens. -/
theorem tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_zariski :
    Transpose.TensorHomEquivNaturalLeft (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace) :=
  tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_ringedSpace S.toRingedSpace

/-- **The bijection of Stacks 08DI on the Zariski site of `S` is dinatural in its internal-Hom
variable.** This is
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.tensorHomEquivDinatural_ringedSpace` at the ringed
space underlying `S`, read at the `tensorHomEquiv` spelling. -/
theorem tensorHomEquivDinatural_zariski :
    Transpose.TensorHomEquivDinatural (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace) :=
  tensorHomEquivDinatural_ringedSpace S.toRingedSpace

end Zariski

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  [PreservesFiniteLimits (associatedModuleOfSheaf B S hS)]

/-- **The structure sheaf `𝒪_S` as an object of `D(𝒪_S)`**, placed in degree zero: the free sheaf
of modules of rank one on the Zariski site of `S`. It is the generator whose thick triangulated
closure case (2) of Stacks 08JP is about.

It is `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedProjectionFormula.singleUnit` of the ringed space underlying `S`,
which is the spelling the right unit constraint of the derived tensor product below
(`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.rightUnitorAtUnit`) and the producer of
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.MixedTranspose.GeneratedByOp` at a strictly perfect
complex (`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.generatedByOp_of_isStrictlyPerfect`) are
stated at. Written out it is
`(DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).obj (SheafOfModules.unit _)`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.zariskiUnitObj`; the two are the same object, and this one is an
`abbrev` at the `singleUnit` spelling so that the instances and producers keyed there apply to it
without an intervening rewrite. -/
abbrev zariskiSingleUnit : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf) :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedProjectionFormula.singleUnit S.toRingedSpace

/-! ### The shift data of the two factors `ε^*` and `Λ` -/

section Factors

attribute [local instance] preservesFiniteLimits_ringedSiteModuleULift
  preservesFiniteColimits_ringedSiteModuleULift

/-- **`ε^*` on derived categories commutes with the shift.** It is
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategory` of the inverse image of sheaves of modules along `ε`,
which is additive, right exact as a left adjoint and left exact by hypothesis, so the shift
commutation is the one `mapDerivedCategory` carries. -/
@[instance_reducible] def commShift_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel :
    (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).CommShift ℤ :=
  inferInstanceAs ((associatedModuleOfSheaf B S hS).mapDerivedCategory.CommShift ℤ)

/-- **`ε^*` on derived categories is triangulated**, being
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategory` of an exact additive functor. -/
theorem isTriangulated_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel :
    letI := commShift_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS
    (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).IsTriangulated :=
  inferInstanceAs ((associatedModuleOfSheaf B S hS).mapDerivedCategory.IsTriangulated)

/-- **The module-universe comparison on derived categories commutes with the shift.** It is
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategory` of the universe lift of module sheaves, which is
additive and exact in both directions. -/
@[instance_reducible] def commShift_derivedModuleULift :
    (derivedModuleULift B S hS).CommShift ℤ :=
  inferInstanceAs ((ringedSiteModuleULift B S hS).mapDerivedCategory.CommShift ℤ)

omit [PreservesFiniteLimits (associatedModuleOfSheaf B S hS)] in
/-- **The module-universe comparison on derived categories is triangulated.** -/
theorem isTriangulated_derivedModuleULift :
    letI := commShift_derivedModuleULift B S hS
    (derivedModuleULift B S hS).IsTriangulated :=
  inferInstanceAs ((ringedSiteModuleULift B S hS).mapDerivedCategory.IsTriangulated)

end Factors

section Comparison

variable
  (T₂ : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)) ×
        DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u}
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)) ⥤
      DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)))
  (e₂ : ∀ (A : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)))
      (K L : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O))),
      (A ⟶ ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).obj (op K)).obj L) ≃
        (T₂.obj (A, K) ⟶ (derivedModuleULift B S hS).obj L))
  (m : internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace ⋙
        derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS ⋙ derivedModuleULift B S hS ≅
      ((derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS ⋙
          derivedModuleULift B S hS).prod
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)) ⋙ T₂)

/-- **The comparison of Stacks 08JP at the standard model, as a natural transformation of its
first argument**, from `E ↦ Λ ε^* R𝓗om_{𝒪_S}(E, F)` to `E ↦ R𝓗om_𝒪(ε^* E, ε^* F)` on
`D(𝒪_S)ᵒᵖ`.

Its components are
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel`, by
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.MixedTranspose.homComparisonNatTrans_app`. It is
built from the two clauses of Stacks 08J8 for each of the two bijections; on the source side both
are proved, and on the target side they are the hypotheses `hn₂` and `hd₂`. In particular the
*existence* of this transformation, and the identification of its components with the comparison,
are no longer hypotheses of the two theorems below. -/
abbrev derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonNatTrans
    (hn₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivNatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hd₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivDinatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (F : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf)) :
    MixedTranspose.comparisonSourceFunctor
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) F ⟶
      MixedTranspose.comparisonTargetFunctor
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
        (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) F :=
  MixedTranspose.homComparisonNatTrans (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
    (derivedModuleULift B S hS) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf)
    (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂
    (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace) e₂ m
    (tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_zariski S) (tensorHomEquivDinatural_zariski S) hn₂ hd₂ F

variable
  (r₂ : ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)),
      T₂.obj (Z, (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).obj
        (zariskiSingleUnit S)) ≅ Z)

/-- **The comparison at the standard model is an isomorphism at every `E` generated by `𝒪_S`.**

This is `MixedTranspose.isIso_homComparison_of_generatedByOp_natTrans` at `ε`: the unit case is the
computation `ε^* R𝓗om(𝒪_S, F) = ε^* F = R𝓗om(ε^*𝒪_S, ε^* F)`, and the dévissage carries it to the
thick triangulated closure of `𝒪_S`.

The source right unitor and its naturality — the `r₁` and `hr₁` the dévissage asks for — are
supplied rather than assumed: they are
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.rightUnitorAtUnit` and
`rightUnitorAtUnit_naturality` at the ringed space underlying `S`. -/
theorem isIso_derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel_natTrans
    (hn₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivNatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hd₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivDinatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hr₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedRightUnitorNatural
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) T₂ (zariskiSingleUnit S) r₂)
    (hm : MixedTranspose.MonoidalityUnital
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ m (zariskiSingleUnit S)
      (rightUnitorAtUnit S.toRingedSpace) r₂)
    (F : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    (hF₁ : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).flip.obj F).CommShift ℤ)
    (hF₁t : letI := hF₁
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).flip.obj F).IsTriangulated)
    (hF₂ : ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).flip.obj
      ((derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).obj F)).CommShift ℤ)
    (hF₂t : letI := hF₂
      ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).flip.obj
        ((derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).obj F)).IsTriangulated)
    (hsh : MixedTranspose.ShiftCompatible
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace) e₂ m
      (commShift_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
      (commShift_derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_zariski S) (tensorHomEquivDinatural_zariski S) hn₂ hd₂ F
      hF₁ hF₂)
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    (hE : MixedTranspose.GeneratedByOp (zariskiSingleUnit S) E) :
    IsIso (derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel B S hS T₂ e₂ m E F) :=
  MixedTranspose.isIso_homComparison_of_generatedByOp_natTrans
    (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS)
    (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace) e₂ m
    (zariskiSingleUnit S) (rightUnitorAtUnit S.toRingedSpace) r₂
    (commShift_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
    (commShift_derivedModuleULift B S hS)
    (isTriangulated_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
    (isTriangulated_derivedModuleULift B S hS)
    (tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_zariski S) (tensorHomEquivDinatural_zariski S)
    (rightUnitorAtUnit_naturality S.toRingedSpace)
    hn₂ hd₂ hr₂ hm F hF₁ hF₁t hF₂ hF₂t hsh E hE

/-- **Stacks 08JP, case (2), over the mixed-universe data `T₂`, `e₂`, `m`.**

The canonical map

`ε^* R𝓗om_{𝒪_S}(E, F) ⟶ R𝓗om_𝒪(ε^* E, ε^* F)`

of `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison`, between the
two sides `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.raisedDerivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHom` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedSheafHomOfAssociatedModule`, is an **isomorphism** whenever
`E` lies in the strictly full saturated triangulated subcategory of `D(𝒪_S)` generated by the
structure sheaf, and `F` is arbitrary — which is the shape of case (2) of Stacks 08JP, whose
hypothesis on `E` is perfection and whose `F` is unrestricted.

The condition on `E` is what takes the statement off `E = 𝒪_S`; it is stronger than 08JP's
perfection, and the module docstring records that no implication from perfection to it can be
proved — the bridge is 08JP's localization step. The conditions on the data are listed there too.
The *source* right unitor and its naturality are not among them: they are discharged at the real
unitor `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.rightUnitorAtUnit`. The two model
identifications are isomorphisms, so the conclusion for the canonical map is the conclusion for the
comparison at the standard model. -/
theorem isIso_derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison_natTrans
    (hn₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivNatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hd₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivDinatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hr₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedRightUnitorNatural
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) T₂ (zariskiSingleUnit S) r₂)
    (hm : MixedTranspose.MonoidalityUnital
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ m (zariskiSingleUnit S)
      (rightUnitorAtUnit S.toRingedSpace) r₂)
    (F : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    (hF₁ : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).flip.obj F).CommShift ℤ)
    (hF₁t : letI := hF₁
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).flip.obj F).IsTriangulated)
    (hF₂ : ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).flip.obj
      ((derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).obj F)).CommShift ℤ)
    (hF₂t : letI := hF₂
      ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).flip.obj
        ((derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).obj F)).IsTriangulated)
    (hsh : MixedTranspose.ShiftCompatible
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace) e₂ m
      (commShift_derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
      (commShift_derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (tensorHomEquivNaturalLeft_zariski S) (tensorHomEquivDinatural_zariski S) hn₂ hd₂ F
      hF₁ hF₂)
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    (hE : MixedTranspose.GeneratedByOp (zariskiSingleUnit S) E) :
    IsIso (derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison B S hS T₂ e₂ m E F) := by
  have h : IsIso (derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel B S hS T₂ e₂ m E F) :=
    isIso_derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel_natTrans B S hS T₂ e₂ m r₂
      hn₂ hd₂ hr₂ hm F hF₁ hF₁t hF₂ hF₂t hsh E hE
  have hinv : IsIso ((derivedModuleULift B S hS).map
      (derivedAssociatedModuleObjModelIso B S hS
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).obj (op E)).obj F)).inv) :=
    Iso.isIso_inv ((derivedModuleULift B S hS).mapIso
      (derivedAssociatedModuleObjModelIso B S hS
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).obj (op E)).obj F)))
  rw [derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison_eq]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso' hinv
    (IsIso.comp_isIso' h (Iso.isIso_hom (derivedSheafHomOfAssociatedModuleModelIso B S hS E F)))

/-- **Stacks 08JP, case (2) at a strictly perfect complex, over the mixed-universe data `T₂`,
`e₂`, `m`.**

If `E` is isomorphic in `D(𝒪_S)` to a strictly perfect complex `P` of `𝒪_S`-modules in the sense
of [Stacks, Tag 08C4] — bounded, with each term a direct summand of a finite free module — then
for arbitrary `F` the canonical map

`ε^* R𝓗om_{𝒪_S}(E, F) ⟶ R𝓗om_𝒪(ε^* E, ε^* F)`

is an isomorphism. This is the previous theorem composed with
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.generatedByOp_of_isStrictlyPerfect`, which puts a
strictly perfect complex in the thick triangulated closure of the structure sheaf, and with the
closure of that property under isomorphisms of `E`.

The hypothesis on `E` is the *global* reading of perfection, so it is the hypothesis of case (2)
of Stacks 08JP *specialised* and not that hypothesis: [Stacks, Tag 08CM] asks for a strictly
perfect model only locally, and here one is asked for on all of `S`. The missing step is the
source's first one, "the question is local on `S`", and it is genuinely missing rather than merely
unformalized in the thick-closure form — see the module docstring for why `perfect ⟹ 𝒪_S`-generated
is a false implication rather than an unproved one. -/
theorem isIso_derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison_isStrictlyPerfect
    (hn₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivNatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hd₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivDinatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hr₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedRightUnitorNatural
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) T₂ (zariskiSingleUnit S) r₂)
    (hm : MixedTranspose.MonoidalityUnital
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ m (zariskiSingleUnit S)
      (rightUnitorAtUnit S.toRingedSpace) r₂)
    (F : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    (hF₁ : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).flip.obj F).CommShift ℤ)
    (hF₁t : letI := hF₁
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).flip.obj F).IsTriangulated)
    (hF₂ : ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).flip.obj
      ((derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).obj F)).CommShift ℤ)
    (hF₂t : letI := hF₂
      ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).flip.obj
